.TH DAYLOG 1
.SH NAME
daylog \- local-first task tracker and daily journal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daylog
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daylog
stores tasks and journal bullets locally in SQLite. It is designed for offline, single-user use.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daylog add DESCRIPTION
Create a task. Use \fB--project\fR, \fB--tag\fR, \fB--due\fR, and \fB--important\fR for metadata.
.TP
.B daylog task list
List active tasks. Add \fB--json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B daylog task important ID
Mark a task important.
.TP
.B daylog task unimportant ID
Clear a task's important flag.
.TP
.B daylog task toggle-important ID
Toggle a task's important flag.
.TP
.B daylog journal add DESCRIPTION
Create a journal bullet.
.TP
.B daylog review done
Mark today's review complete.
.TP
.B daylog config show
Show local configuration.
.TP
.B daylog doctor
Check the local database and data directory.
.TP
.B daylog remind install
Write the platform reminder scheduler configuration.
.TP
.B daylog data export
Print a lossless-readable JSON snapshot of current task and journal records.
.TP
.B daylog data backup
Create a timestamped local database backup.
.TP
.B daylog data import FILE
Preview or apply a JSON snapshot. Use \fB--apply\fR and resolve conflicts with \fB--prefer-import\fR or \fB--prefer-local\fR.
.TP
.B daylog search [QUERY]
Search task and journal records. Filter with \fB--project\fR, \fB--tag\fR, \fB--status\fR, and \fB--date\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.daylog/daylog.db
The default SQLite database.
.TP
.B DAYLOG_DATA_DIR
Environment variable overriding the data directory.
.SH NOTES
The complete TUI, reminders, import/export, and backup workflows are documented as they are implemented.
